      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-11-30_WidnesExaminer_art0094" n="art0094">
        <head>Town Council.</head>
        <p>Town Council.</p>
        <p>The monthly meeting of the Town Council w'll be held on Tuesday evening at 6 o'clock.</p>
        <p>Pcrsuc BENEFIT --TINDSR, TRH CLOCit feklll. C BOOTS IN LANCA.SHERS.—AdVt.</p>
        <p>Alderman Fairclough's Resignation. We regret to state that Alderman James Fairclough whose resignation from the Town Council will be laid before the Council on Tuesday, is lying seriously ill at his residence, Gatesgarth, Latchford. Alderman Fairclough has been continuously in office since the year 1891 and filled the office of Mayor in 1891-5-6-7. He has been a valuable member and will be much missed from the Council.</p>
        <p>'LINSEED CONIPOUND' for Coughs and Colds. Of proven efficacy. Of Chemists.—Advt. Messrs. Crosfield's Band. The members of the above band held a smoking concert on Wednesday evening in the girls' dining</p>
        <p>room in the works, in- connection with tlie presenta: tion to the Hon. Sec., Mr. J. Taylor, of a (Told chain and medal, which had been subscribed for .by the</p>
        <p>members of the band and committee in recognition of services to the band since 1901. Mr. F. J. Lord made</p>
        <p>the presentation,and was supported by Mr.W.Halli well (conductor), Mr. Taylor suitably responding. Mr. J. Forster presided at the piano and songs were contri- buted by several members of the band.</p>
        <p>PUBLIC BENEFIT.—IINDER THE CLOCK FOR BEST BOOTS IN LANCASHIRE.—Advt. Election Expenses. The folio cving returns of expenses incurred in the recent municipal elections have been received by the Town Clerk :—Councillor J. Skelland, 3s. ; Councillor</p>
        <p>T. Burton, £1 78 6d. ; Alderman Ellison, nil ; Mr. G. T. Wilding, £l4 4s. ; Councillor J. Fulton-Smith, £4 ss. ; Councillor William Rogers, £26 16s. 6d. ; Councillor W. B. Roberts, £32 38. 3d.; Mr. W. Clegg, £8 Bs. 3d. ; Councillor J. T. Locker, £5 ; Councillor J. Hawthorn, £1 10s. 6d. ; Councillor J. Wilkinson,</p>
        <p>11 Bs. 6d. 'LINSEED COMPOUND' for Coughs, Colds, and Bronchial troubles. 9id. &amp; 1/11. Of Chemists. —Advt</p>
      </div>
