        <p>' amiTorer - -</p>
        <p>by these monthly gatherings are to minutes of the previous meeting, a, sheet (I believe annually) and perioc officials who consistently continue to good work neglected by their pred their retirement, have a hearty vote of to them for services not rendered. glaring example (to adopt the lines poet) of</p>
        <p>formally pass the ccept the balance- lically select new ) leave undone the lecessors, who on ,f thanks accorded Here, Sir, is a of a well-known</p>
        <p>Nothing attempted, nothing done They deserve a Long repose. ONLOOKER. JOHN WOR,EMAN AND MR. C. E. PARR. We have been compelled to hold John Workman's reply to Mr.C.E.Psrker over till next week.—En."Ex."</p>
