      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-11-30_WidnesExaminer_art0113" n="art0113">
        <head>BROKEN</head>
        <p>BROKEN</p>
        <p>SLEEP.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON PROOF,</p>
        <p>Mr. H. Thomas, 97, Fox-street, Warrington, says:—" I have suffered with kidney complaint more or less all my life. It is in the family. Every now and then I would have to knock off work and stay at home until the violence of the pains in the small of my back had worn off sufficiently for me to start work</p>
        <p>again.</p>
        <p>"The urinary system was out of order, the kidney secretions being thick and at times co'ntained gravel.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-11-30_WidnesExaminer_art0114" n="art0114">
        <head>HINTS FOR THE HOME.</head>
        <p>HINTS FOR THE HOME.</p>
        <p>teture Tells a Story</p>
        <p>There were also headaches and giddiness sometimes severely.</p>
        <p>"I tried Doan's backache kidney pills and they proved highly beneficial in my case ; they cleared the kidney secretions and eased the pains in my back. I've been first rate since using the medicine. (Signed) Harry Thomas."</p>
        <p>Doan's Backache Kidney Pills are two shillings and ninepence per box (six boxes for thirteen shillings and ninepence.) Of all chemists and stores, or post free, direct from the Foster-McClellan Co., 8, W9lls-street, Oxford-street, London, W. Doan's are (he pills that cured Mr. Thomas.</p>
        <p>=CZ Ti alj• imrro rril7.7rt rogetner wirli iresti air and exercise will ensure a good temper and prevent one from suffering from a torpid liver.</p>
        <p>THE USES OF OLIVE OIL.</p>
        <p>Medical authorities are agreed as to the bene- ficial and remedial effects of olive oil, declaringit as specially useful in any defects of the excre- tory ducts, or arly low state of the system when in need of a tissue-building food. It has long been observed that those who use olive oil as a common article of food are generally healthier and in better condition than those who do not. It is said to be destructive to certain forms of micro-organic life, and for the eradication of such from the system it is frequently advised by physicians for internal use.</p>
