ch seemed to leave a reflection that if the Board had mild, he says, if erroneous 'judicial " methods obtained, surely the Clerk was the one at fault. Mr. Suttonsays energetically considered the matter and dealt firm! that had he been in Court ho would have sought to with it, the probability was that the slander case would avoid rebuke by saving that he bad not at any time not have come before the Court. been present during plaintiff's statements to the Mr. Jolley moved "Teat the Clark he instructed to Guardians, inform the Local Government Board of the result of the action and of the circumstances which led up to it and to ask the Local Government Board to inquire into the administration of the Union Hospital and to decide whether Dr. Flitcroft shall retain his office." Sympathy with Dr. Flitcroft. I,•~Maimm.4 At a meeting of the Warrington Board of Guardians Woods' Great Peppermint Cure, for Coughs and on Wednesday, the Clerk said he had received the fol. Colds; never fails. 1/11, 2/9.—Advt. lowing letter from Dr. Harold Joseph :—Dear Sir, will</p>
